### Space Orchestrator (Brain of the Space)

**[FIX — god-object]** The original Orchestrator was a single box doing seven unrelated jobs (understand, plan, build team, allocate resources, monitor, adapt, reflect). That's not one component, it's a pipeline. It is now split into five sub-modules with a defined handoff, so each piece can be built, tested, and replaced independently:

| Sub-module | Responsibility | Input | Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Goal Analyzer** | Turns a raw Command into a structured Goal Spec + constraints. **[FIX P2-9]** Also classifies the shape of the resulting Task Graph and stamps the Goal Spec `single_agent_eligible: bool` — see [§18](#18-when-is-a-space-worth-it). | Command | Goal Spec |
| **Planner** | Produces a versioned Task Graph from the Goal Spec (`plan_version` starts at `1`). | Goal Spec | Task Graph |
| **Team Builder** | Maps Task Graph nodes to Agents/Workers/Skills, requests Resource grants. **[FIX P2-9]** If the Goal Spec is `single_agent_eligible`, may assign one Agent + Skills for the whole graph and skip full team construction. | Task Graph | Assignment Table |
| **Monitor** | Subscribes to Pulses, tracks task/resource state, detects drift or failure, and is the single source of truth for **which `plan_version` is currently authoritative**. | Pulses | Status Events |
| **Adapter / Reflector** | On Status Events, re-plans (emitting a **Plan Delta**, never an in-place mutation), retries, or escalates; on completion, writes Experience back to Space Memory (subject to [Cross-Space Promotion](#cross-space-knowledge-promotion) if the target is global). | Status Events | Plan Deltas, Experience Records |

The Orchestrator itself is now a thin coordinator that sequences these five modules — it holds no business logic of its own.

