## 6. Pulse Bus (Nervous System)

*Every component publishes & subscribes to Pulses.*

The Pulse Bus connects the Space Kernel to every functional layer (Cognitive, Execution, Skills, Tools, Workflow, Adaptation) and out to the Extensibility and Communication layers.

**[FIX P0-1 — typed registry + failure taxonomy]** `Pulse.type` is no longer a free-text string. It is a dot-namespaced enum validated against the [Pulse Type Registry](#pulse-type-registry) at publish time — **an unknown `type` is rejected synchronously by the Bus with a protocol-level error to the publisher, not admitted as a Pulse.** This keeps the rejection out of the Pulse stream itself and avoids an infinite-regress "invalid Pulse about an invalid Pulse."

Every Pulse also carries:
- `severity: info | warning | error | critical`
- `parent_pulse_id` — the immediate causal parent, alongside the existing `correlation_id` which ties the whole chain back to one originating Command.

✅ **Done:** from any Pulse, walk `parent_pulse_id` back to root to reconstruct the exact causal chain; cross-check against `correlation_id` to confirm it belongs to the same Command.

**[FIX P1-6]** A Pulse whose payload originated from untrusted external content also carries `taint: bool`, which propagates down the `parent_pulse_id` chain — see [Prompt-Injection & Taint Model](#prompt-injection--taint-model).

