## 9. Cross-Cutting Services

- **Event / Pulse Bus** — nervous system of Ryu; enforces the [Pulse Type Registry](#pulse-type-registry) at publish time.
- **Registry Service** — Agents, Workers, Skills, Tools, Nodes, MCP, Models. **[FIX — capability-provider risk tiers]** Tool and Skill registrations include `risk_tier: low | high`, set at registration time and immutable without a human action recorded as a `security.grant.approved` Pulse. A high-risk Tool follows the same rule as a high-risk Node capability: every `CapabilityRequest` requires fresh human re-approval regardless of taint state. The trade-off is that a risk reclassification cannot be self-service.
  - ✅ **Done =** attempting to register or mutate a Tool or Skill without a `risk_tier`, or to change its `risk_tier` without a corresponding human-approved `security.grant.approved` Pulse, is rejected by the Registry Service.
- **[FIX — signed capability supply chain]** Tool and Skill registrations are signed, versioned, and content-addressed. `risk_tier` binds to `content_hash`: a different payload is a different, unclassified registration and cannot inherit the prior registration's tier. Community Plugin entries must be signed; the Registry rejects unsigned entries. Spaces reference `skill_id@version`, never `@latest`.
  - ✅ **Done =** swapping a Skill's payload without a new registration cannot inherit its old `risk_tier`, and a Space cannot resolve an unpinned Skill reference.
- **Cost & Usage Tracker** — tokens, cost, budget; feeds live spend to the Space Kernel's [Admission Control](#admission-control-budget-enforcement), which is the actual enforcement point.
- **Resource Manager** — CPU, GPU, RAM, Disk, Network. **[FIX P1-7 — concurrency resolution, answers Open Question]** This is the single decision-maker for contested Resources. Model chosen: **queue with lease**, not first-writer-wins and not per-Agent locks (locks are allowed only as a local optimization *within* one Agent's own exclusive sub-tasks, never across Agents).
  - **Resource identity** is `(resource_type, provider_id, instance_id)` — never a human-readable name. Two requests for "the GPU" can resolve to different instances; only the Manager-issued instance handle is authoritative.
  - A request for a free Resource gets an immediate `Lease` (see [§16](#lease)). A request for a leased Resource is queued FIFO by arrival timestamp at the Manager (or Space-defined priority order); the loser receives a `resource.conflict` Pulse with its queue position — never silence.
  - ✅ **Done:** two Agents racing for one GPU capability get a defined outcome (first accepted request wins the lease) and the loser is informed via `resource.conflict`.
- **Sandbox Manager** — isolation, permissions, security; the enforcement point for the [Prompt-Injection & Taint Model](#prompt-injection--taint-model) at the Worker boundary.

