## 12. Core Runtime (Shared Across All Spaces)

Runtime Engine (Event Loop) · Lifecycle Manager (Init, Start, Stop) · Component Registry (Discover, Register) · Context Manager (Scopes, Windows) · Pulse Bus (Publish / Subscribe) · Configuration (Env, Secrets) · Sandbox (Isolation) · Resource Manager (Allocation) · Rate Limiter (Per Space) · Cost Tracker (Tokens, $) · Utilities & Base Classes

### LLM Call Recording (contract v0)

**[FIX — reproducible LLM traces]** Every LLM call's full input and output is persisted as a record keyed by `correlation_id`, alongside the Pulse stream. Recorded conversations live in the Space timeline; retention is a per-Space policy in Settings & Limits. This enables reproducible debugging by replaying exact model inputs and frozen traces for the Adaptation Layer's Evaluation module. Contract v0 deliberately defers retention and evaluation design to empirical results.

### Rate Limiter Contract

**[FIX — per-Space backpressure]** The Rate Limiter enforces per-Space token/sec and tool-call/sec budgets. On exceed, it queues requests with backpressure and publishes `rate.limited` at `severity: info`; it never silently drops a request, and this is not an error in the Failure Taxonomy. The per-Space Rate Limiter composes above the global Resource Manager: Space-level budgets gate first, then the Manager arbitrates whatever passes.

✅ **Done =** an over-budget Space receives `rate.limited` Pulses and queued dispatch, never silent drops, and never pollutes the Failure Taxonomy.

### Context Manager Contract

**[FIX P1-5 — context management contract]** The original map named a Context Manager but never defined its job. Defined here:

- **Scope:** three nested windows — per-Task (narrowest, one Task Graph node), per-Agent (a working session across several Tasks), per-Space (the shared Cognitive Workspace, §4). Each Agent reads its own window plus pinned shared state; it does not see other Agents' raw windows.
- **Window size:** bounded by `model_max_context − reserved_completion_tokens − safety_margin`. Content is either **pinned** (Goal Spec, current Task, `plan_version`, last 3 decisions, open Plan Deltas — never evicted) or **evictable** (older turns, superseded tool output).
- **Eviction policy:** LRU over evictable content only.
- **Compaction trigger:** when window utilization crosses a threshold (default 80%), the Context Manager compacts — it summarizes evicted content into a structured **Handoff Note** (`{goal, current_task_id, plan_version, last_3_decisions, open_questions}`) and writes it to Space Memory's Working Context.
- **Recovery after compaction:** an Agent resuming after compaction reads the Handoff Note, not the raw evicted history.
- **Subagent pattern:** for long chains, or when a Task Graph node is independently decomposable, the Team Builder spawns a fresh **Subagent Worker** (Execution Layer, §7) seeded *only* with the Handoff Note and its relevant plan node — not the parent's full history. This bounds context growth structurally instead of relying on ever-larger windows.

✅ **Done:** a 500-turn task runs without a context-overflow failure, and immediately after compaction the Agent can state the goal, its current task, and the last 3 decisions — because those are exactly the fields pinned in the Handoff Note.

