| 2026-09-11 | **Idempotency / duplicate side effects on retry** | `CapabilityRequest.idempotency_key`; a retry with the same key returns the original `CapabilityResponse`, never re-executes. See [§16](#component-contracts) and [§10 — Failure Escalation Flow](#failure-escalation-flow). |
| 2026-09-11 | **In-place plan mutation / no versioning** | `TaskGraph.plan_version` + `PlanDelta` diffs, applied via single-writer compare-and-swap at the Kernel. In-flight tasks on a superseded version: `finish`, `checkpoint`, or `cancel`, decided per-node by the Delta. See [§16](#task-graph--plan-delta). |
| 2026-09-11 | **No context management contract** | Context Manager: three nested scopes, LRU eviction of non-pinned content, compaction at 80% utilization into a structured Handoff Note, Subagent Worker spawn for long/decomposable chains. See [§12](#context-manager-contract). |
| 2026-09-11 | **No prompt-injection defense** | Tool/Channel output is untrusted data, enforced at the Worker boundary; `taint` propagates on Pulses; low-risk grants auto-approve in-session, high-risk always re-approve, tainted chains block all new grants pending human confirmation. See [Prompt-Injection & Taint Model](#prompt-injection--taint-model). |
| 2026-09-11 | **No "single agent vs. Space" boundary** | Goal Analyzer stamps `single_agent_eligible`; Team Builder may skip team construction. Boundary condition and token-cost trade-off stated explicitly. See [§18](#18-when-is-a-space-worth-it). |
| 2026-09-11 | **MCP positioning unclear** | MCP is the extensibility wire protocol (Linux Foundation Agentic AI Foundation standard). MCP Tools → Tools Layer, MCP Resources → Space Memory, MCP Prompts → Prompts & Templates. See [§5](#5-extensibility-layer). |
| 2026-09-11 | **Auditable taint clearance** | `security.taint.cleared` records human clearance by `correlation_id`; clearance is forward-only, so pre-clear Pulses retain `taint: true` and the audit history remains reconstructable. `security.grant.approved` records human approval for high-risk grants. See [§10](#prompt-injection--taint-model) and [§16](#payload-schemas). |
| 2026-09-11 | **Risk tiers for all capability providers** | Tool and Skill registrations carry immutable `risk_tier: low | high`; a change requires human action recorded as `security.grant.approved`. High-risk Tools and Node capabilities require fresh human re-approval for every request, regardless of taint. See [§9](#9-cross-cutting-services) and [§16](#component-contracts). |
| 2026-09-11 | **Pulse payload schemas and escalation windows** | Every registered `Pulse.type` has a required payload schema. `space.budget.exceeded.window_id` identifies the Kernel-generated escalation window and is renewed on human acknowledgement or budget replenishment, enforcing one escalation per window. See [§4](#admission-control-budget-enforcement) and [§16](#payload-schemas). |
| 2026-09-11 | **SecretRef containment** | `CapabilityRequest.params` carries `secret://` references, never raw secrets; the Sandbox Manager resolves them only inside the execution sandbox, and the Bus/schema validator rejects resolved secrets in every Pulse field. See [§10](#prompt-injection--taint-model) and [§16](#component-contracts). |
